Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.20,0:00:04.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,At 9:41 tonight, every search you've ever made goes public.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.80,0:00:06.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,For everyone. All at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.60,0:00:12.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,At first, it's funny. He searched: how to seem interesting on a date.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.20,0:00:16.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,She searched: how to leave a date early.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.80,0:00:20.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,Then your boss can see it. Your family. Strangers.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.40,0:00:23.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,So people stop searching.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.40,0:00:25.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,Even when they need it most.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.80,0:00:32.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,No one looks up a scary symptom. No one asks how to leave a bad relationship.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.60,0:00:35.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,Questions that could have helped… go unasked.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.80,0:00:41.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,Weeks later, people realize everyone's history is weird… and the shame starts to fade.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.60,0:00:47.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,If every search became public… would you still dare to ask?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.20,0:00:03.00,Note,,0,0,0,,FICTION · WHAT IF?
